Content sourcing for Daily Insights
------------------------------------
Use Sym-authored or licensed wellness copy only (see docs/daily-insights-sources.md).
Do NOT scrape patient.info or other clinical publishers without written permission —
their terms typically forbid commercial crawling / reuse for apps and datasets.
Expand the catalog via utils/dailyInsightSeedData.js or licensed imports.

1. General health ⭐

Probably your most important category.

Use it for:

Daily wellness insights
Energy and lifestyle
Healthy routines
General preventive health education
Understanding how habits affect wellbeing
2. Healthy living ⭐

Excellent fit for SymWellness.

Use it for:

Sleep habits
Physical activity
Hydration
Stress management
Healthy routines
Preventive lifestyle recommendations
3. Diet and nutrition ⭐

Very relevant if your app provides nutrition and wellness insights.

Use it for:

Healthy eating
Balanced diets
Food education
Vitamins and nutrients
Hydration
General nutrition insights
4. Weight loss management ⭐

Only include this if you want weight management to remain an important feature.

Frame it around:

Healthy weight goals
Sustainable habits
Activity
Nutrition
Progress tracking

Avoid positioning it as treatment for obesity or medical weight-loss management.

5. Mental health ⚠️ Selectively

You can use content related to:

Stress management
Mindfulness
Relaxation
Sleep
Emotional wellbeing

However, I would not build SymWellness around diagnosing or treating mental health conditions.

You could internally frame this section in your app as Mindfulness & Wellbeing rather than "Mental Health."

6. Bones, joints and muscles ⚠️ Selectively

Useful for preventive wellness content such as:

Mobility
Stretching
Posture
Exercise
Muscle recovery
Staying active

Avoid disease-specific or injury-treatment content.

7. Heart health and blood vessels ⚠️ Preventive content only

This can be useful for general prevention:

Exercise
Healthy eating
Sleep
Stress
Heart-healthy lifestyle habits

But avoid turning SymWellness into a cardiovascular disease management app.

8. Digestive health ⚠️ Selectively

Good for general wellness insights:

Gut-friendly nutrition
Hydration
Fiber
Healthy eating habits

Avoid content focused heavily on diagnosing digestive diseases.